0
00:00:00,968 --> 00:00:04,137
Tyra: PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"...

1
00:00:04,137 --> 00:00:06,707
THE GIRLS WERE OVERWHELMED
WHEN THEY WERE FLOWN TO PARIS.

2
00:00:06,707 --> 00:00:09,009
Adrianne: THIS IS
SO BEAUTIFUL.

3
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:10,744
Tyra: SHANNON'S FANTASY
BECAME A REALITY...

4
00:00:10,744 --> 00:00:13,046
Shannon: OH, MY WORD!

5
00:00:13,046 --> 00:00:15,148
Tyra: WHEN SHE MET
THE MAN OF HER DREAMS.

6
00:00:15,148 --> 00:00:18,252
THE RIFT WIDENED BETWEEN ROBIN
AND SOME OF THE GIRLS.

7
00:00:18,252 --> 00:00:19,186
Adrianne: HOW DO YOU SAY,
"ADRIANNE HAS

8
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:20,487
ENORMOUS CHA-CHAS"?

9
00:00:20,487 --> 00:00:21,388
Robin: I DON'T SPEAK
LIKE THAT.

10
00:00:21,388 --> 00:00:22,189
I DON'T ACT LIKE THAT.

11
00:00:22,189 --> 00:00:24,091
I DON'T WANNA HEAR THAT.

12
00:00:24,091 --> 00:00:27,127
Tyra: AND EVERYONE WAS SAD
WHEN KESSE WAS ASKED TO LEAVE.

13
00:00:27,127 --> 00:00:30,731
Robin: KESSE AND MYSELF,
YOU KNOW, USED TO READ--

14
00:00:30,731 --> 00:00:33,066
USED TO READ THE BIBLE TOGETHER.

15
00:00:33,066 --> 00:00:36,637
♪♪♪

16
00:01:15,742 --> 00:01:17,244
Adrianne: OH.

17
00:01:17,244 --> 00:01:20,347
Elyse: COME ON, ADRIANNE.

18
00:01:20,347 --> 00:01:22,482
Man: (speaking indistinctly)

19
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:53,981
Robin: WHEN MISS KESSE LEFT,
IT WAS HURTFUL TO SEE HER GO.

20
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:57,584
I PHYSICALLY COULDN'T STAND UP.

21
00:01:57,584 --> 00:01:59,119
I REMEMBER LEANING ON THE WALLS
AND I REMEMBER

22
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:00,287
GOING TO SIT DOWN.

23
00:02:00,287 --> 00:02:01,755
SHE REMINDED ME OF MY SISTER.

24
00:02:01,755 --> 00:02:03,657
WE WERE SORORITY SISTERS.

25
00:02:03,657 --> 00:02:06,093
WE WERE BOTH FROM THE SOUTH,
ROOMMATES, CHRISTIANS.

26
00:02:06,093 --> 00:02:08,061
SHE WAS MY BEST FRIEND
IN THIS SITUATION.

27
00:02:09,997 --> 00:02:11,732
Shannon: I FELT LIKE
A LITTLE PIECE OF ME WENT AWAY

28
00:02:11,732 --> 00:02:13,367
BECAUSE KESSE WAS PROBABLY
ONE OF THE GIRLS THAT

29
00:02:13,367 --> 00:02:16,169
I'VE HUNG OUT WITH THE MOST
BESIDES ROBIN.

30
00:02:16,536 --> 00:02:19,406
Adrianne: I BELIEVE
IN A HIGHER POWER.

31
00:02:19,406 --> 00:02:20,507
I DON'T BELIEVE
THAT HIGHER POWER

32
00:02:20,507 --> 00:02:24,177
ASKS YOU TO SACRIFICE
YOUR EVERY DAMN MOMENT.

33
00:02:24,177 --> 00:02:25,612
I DO BELIEVE IN GOD.

34
00:02:25,612 --> 00:02:28,215
I'M JUST NOT PSYCHOTIC ABOUT IT.

35
00:02:28,215 --> 00:02:31,251
I HATE HOW ROBIN ROLLS HER EYES
AT ME WHEN I'M, LIKE, PRAYING.

36
00:02:31,251 --> 00:02:33,587
I'LL BE SITTING THERE PRAYING
FOR MY GRANDMA OR SOMETHING,

37
00:02:33,587 --> 00:02:36,289
AND SHE'LL LOOK OVER AT ME
AND ROLL HER EYES.

38
00:02:43,697 --> 00:02:45,265
Elyse: THINGS WOULD HAVE
DEFINITELY SUCKED

39
00:02:45,265 --> 00:02:49,102
IF MY CLOSEST ALLY IN THE HOUSE
HAD BEEN ELIMINATED,

40
00:02:49,102 --> 00:02:51,638
AND I'M REALLY, REALLY GLAD
THAT ADRIANNE STAYED ON.

41
00:02:51,638 --> 00:02:52,739
Adrianne: BOO-YAH.

42
00:02:52,739 --> 00:02:55,375
♪♪♪

43
00:02:59,179 --> 00:03:00,614
Tyra: I'M GONNA MAKE YOU
MORE EDGY, SHANNON.

44
00:03:00,614 --> 00:03:02,215
Shannon: THANKS.

45
00:03:02,215 --> 00:03:04,317
Tyra: I'VE BEEN PHOTOGRAPHED
BY EVERY TOP PHOTOGRAPHER

46
00:03:04,317 --> 00:03:06,353
IN THE WORLD,
AND I'VE TAKEN POINTERS

47
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:07,988
FROM EVERY SINGLE ONE OF THEM.

48
00:03:07,988 --> 00:03:10,357
THAT'S WHY I DECIDED TO SHOOT
THE GIRLS MYSELF--

49
00:03:10,357 --> 00:03:12,759
TO SEE WHAT THE GIRLS LOOK LIKE
THROUGH MY LENS AND HOW THEY

50
00:03:12,759 --> 00:03:16,163
CONNECT WITH THE PHOTOGRAPHER.

51
00:03:16,163 --> 00:03:17,564
THAT IS SO GORGEOUS, ELYSE.

52
00:03:17,564 --> 00:03:20,033
Elyse: NOW THAT FEWER
AND FEWER GIRLS ARE LEFT,

53
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:21,101
I'M STARTING TO TAKE
THE COMPETITION

54
00:03:21,101 --> 00:03:23,036
MUCH MORE SERIOUSLY.

55
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:25,505
I LOVE THAT.

56
00:03:26,073 --> 00:03:27,374
THERE YOU GO.

57
00:03:27,374 --> 00:03:28,742
Shannon: IT IS
A LOT OF PRESSURE

58
00:03:28,742 --> 00:03:30,744
BECAUSE, UM, THE FOUR OF US
THAT ARE LEFT IN THE HOUSE

59
00:03:30,744 --> 00:03:33,180
ARE, LIKE, STARING OUR DREAM
RIGHT IN THE FACE.

60
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:34,548
Tyra: STAY THERE.

61
00:03:34,548 --> 00:03:36,049
WHEN I WAS PHOTOGRAPHING
THE GIRLS, I FELT LIKE

62
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:38,585
THEY WERE FINALLY REALIZING
THE POSSIBILITY OF BECOMING

63
00:03:38,585 --> 00:03:39,352
A MAJOR STAR.

64
00:03:42,656 --> 00:03:44,224
OKAY.

65
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:46,326
Adrianne: THEY'RE REALLY
NARROWING IT DOWN TO WHO HAS

66
00:03:46,326 --> 00:03:48,729
WHAT IT TAKES TO BE A TOP MODEL
AND WHO DOESN'T.

67
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:54,735
♪♪♪

68
00:03:54,735 --> 00:03:57,237
Tyra: IT'S ALL ABOUT PROFILE
AND LOOKING TO THE SKY

69
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:58,972
AND FEELING LIKE AN ANGEL.

70
00:03:58,972 --> 00:04:01,041
Robin: WHAT COMES WITH THIS
IS POWER.

71
00:04:01,041 --> 00:04:04,177
THE RIGHT PERSON CAN USE THIS
AS A MODEM TO TOUCH PEOPLE,

72
00:04:04,177 --> 00:04:07,681
TO MAKE CHANGE.

73
00:04:07,681 --> 00:04:08,515
Tyra: ALL RIGHT,
WE GOT YOU, ROBIN.

74
00:04:08,515 --> 00:04:10,150
Robin: YES, MA'AM.

75
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:14,287
♪♪♪

76
00:04:20,694 --> 00:04:22,496
Tyra: WE TOOK THE GIRLS
TO THE HOUSE OF CARVEN, WHICH IS

77
00:04:22,496 --> 00:04:27,267
THE OLDEST COUTURE HOUSE
IN ALL OF PARIS.

78
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:28,602
Shannon: NOW THIS IS
MY FAVORITE THING.

79
00:04:28,602 --> 00:04:30,270
NO LIE.

80
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:32,706
THE CLOTHES--THERE'S LIKE--
BESIDES BEING EXPENSIVE,

81
00:04:32,706 --> 00:04:34,441
THEY'RE SOME
OF THE NEATEST CLOTHES.

82
00:04:34,441 --> 00:04:36,176
Tyra: HELLO!

83
00:04:36,176 --> 00:04:37,744
Shannon: BONJOUR.

84
00:04:37,744 --> 00:04:39,012
Tyra: AS YOU GUYS KNOW,
PARIS IS THE FASHION CAPITAL

85
00:04:39,012 --> 00:04:41,148
OF THE WORLD
AND THE FASHION CAPITAL

86
00:04:41,148 --> 00:04:43,250
OF COUTURE MODELING.

87
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:45,318
COUTURE IS THE EPITOME
OF FASHION.

88
00:04:45,318 --> 00:04:48,155
A LOT OF TIMES COUTURE CLOTHING
WILL BE ONE OF A KIND.

89
00:04:48,155 --> 00:04:51,158
YOU GUYS NOTICE HOW I HAVE
YOUR HAIR PULLED BACK IN A BUN.

90
00:04:51,158 --> 00:04:53,326
IN FRANCE, THAT'S CALLED
A CHIGNON.

91
00:04:53,326 --> 00:04:55,595
A CHIGNON IS THE MOST ELEGANT
WAY TO WEAR YOUR HAIR,

92
00:04:55,595 --> 00:04:57,464
AND IT'S IMPORTANT
THAT YOUR HAIR IN NO WAY

93
00:04:57,464 --> 00:05:00,000
DISTRACTS FROM THE CLOTHES,
AND TOMORROW YOU'LL BE TESTED

94
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,535
ON YOUR ABILITY
TO CARRY YOURSELF

95
00:05:01,535 --> 00:05:03,670
IN A COUTURE SITUATION.

96
00:05:03,670 --> 00:05:05,372
TODAY YOU'RE GONNA MEET
THE ARTISTIC DIRECTOR OF CARVEN.

97
00:05:05,372 --> 00:05:08,508
PASCAL? (speaks French)
Pascal: WELCOME.

98
00:05:08,508 --> 00:05:10,577
WELCOME TO CARVEN
AND WELCOME TO PARIS.

99
00:05:10,577 --> 00:05:13,079
WELCOME TO THE MAGICAL WORLD
OF HAUTE COUTURE.

100
00:05:23,723 --> 00:05:27,394
♪♪♪

101
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:42,108
Tyra: MUCH BETTER.

102
00:05:42,108 --> 00:05:42,709
Shannon: YOU GOTTA
BE KIDDING ME.

103
00:05:42,709 --> 00:05:44,311
I'M WEARING THESE DRESSES.

104
00:05:44,311 --> 00:05:46,112
THESE DRESSES ARE PROBABLY
MORE EXPENSIVE THAN EVERYTHING

105
00:05:46,112 --> 00:05:47,981
THAT I OWN PERSONALLY.

106
00:05:47,981 --> 00:05:50,450
Adrianne: THE GOWN
WAS, LIKE, A $20,000 GOWN.

107
00:05:50,450 --> 00:05:52,285
HOW ARE YOU NOT GONNA LIKE
SOME GOWN THAT'S WORTH MORE

108
00:05:52,285 --> 00:05:53,453
THAN YOUR HOUSE AND YOUR CAR?

109
00:05:56,756 --> 00:05:59,492
Pascal: THEY'RE ALL VERY
PROFESSIONAL.

110
00:05:59,492 --> 00:06:02,696
I THINK IT WILL BE TOUGH
TO FIND THE WINNER.

111
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:05,265
Shannon: THERE'S ONLY
ONE WINNER, AND SO WHO KNOWS?

112
00:06:05,265 --> 00:06:07,300
IT'S GETTING PRETTY CLOSE,
AND HOPEFULLY, YOU KNOW,

113
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,970
I WILL MAKE IT TO THE TOP.

114
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:12,372
Pascal: GIVE YOU
A SMALL SOUVENIR OF CARVEN.

115
00:06:12,372 --> 00:06:14,040
Shannon: OH,
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

116
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:16,209
(gasps) I SPRAYED THIS ON ME
WHEN I FIRST CAME IN.

117
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:18,612
THANK YOU.

118
00:06:18,612 --> 00:06:20,046
MERCI BEAUCOUP.

119
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:25,218
♪♪♪

120
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:27,520
Adrianne: "TOMORROW IS
YOUR DAY.

121
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:30,390
YOU HAVE FROM 10 TO 3 TO ENJOY
PARIS AND ALL THE SPLENDORS

122
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:32,425
IT HAS TO OFFER."

123
00:06:32,425 --> 00:06:35,061
Elyse: WE GOT A TYRA MAIL
SAYING THAT THE NEXT DAY

124
00:06:35,061 --> 00:06:37,697
WE WOULD HAVE SOME FREE TIME TO
DO WHATEVER WE WANTED ALL DAY.

125
00:06:37,697 --> 00:06:40,300
Adrianne: EIFFEL TOWER,
MOTHER...

126
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:41,635
Shannon: SHOPPING.

127
00:06:41,635 --> 00:06:44,070
Adrianne: YOU GUYS
WANNA GO SHOPPING?

128
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:46,640
I REALLY DON'T LIKE TO SHOP,
AND IT GETS REALLY OLD

129
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:48,441
AFTER, LIKE, AN HOUR.

130
00:06:48,441 --> 00:06:49,743
Shannon: I THOUGHT
YOU WANTED TO GO.

131
00:06:49,743 --> 00:06:51,711
Adrianne: I DON'T HAVE MONEY
TO GO SHOPPING.

132
00:06:51,711 --> 00:06:54,547
I JUST WANNA GO SEE
JIM MORRISON'S GRAVE.

133
00:06:54,547 --> 00:06:56,583
Robin: WHO IS JIM MORRIS,
ADRIANNE?

134
00:06:56,583 --> 00:06:58,618
Adrianne: HE IS
THE LEAD SINGER OF THE DOORS,

135
00:06:58,618 --> 00:07:01,121
ONE OF THE MOST INFLUENTIAL
BANDS THAT HAS EVER EXISTED

136
00:07:01,121 --> 00:07:02,689
ON THE FACE OF THE EARTH.

137
00:07:02,689 --> 00:07:04,991
Elyse: ADRIANNE WANTED
TO GO SEE JIM MORRISON'S GRAVE,

138
00:07:04,991 --> 00:07:07,060
AND SHE WANTED TO GO UP
THE TOP OF THE EIFFEL TOWER,

139
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:09,062
AND ROBIN AND SHANNON
WANTED TO GO SHOPPING.

140
00:07:09,062 --> 00:07:10,163
Shannon: SHE'S WILLING
TO GO SHOPPING WITH US.

141
00:07:10,163 --> 00:07:11,498
WE SHOULD DO SOMETHING
FOR HER, TOO.

142
00:07:11,498 --> 00:07:13,633
Elyse: WE HAVE TO COMPROMISE
SO WE CAN STAY TOGETHER,

143
00:07:13,633 --> 00:07:15,368
BECAUSE I DON'T WANT TO
SPLIT OFF INTO TWO GROUPS.

144
00:07:15,368 --> 00:07:17,504
Robin: I WANNA GO SHOPPING.

145
00:07:17,504 --> 00:07:18,638
Elyse: I THINK
WE CAN ALL COMPROMISE

146
00:07:18,638 --> 00:07:20,140
SO WE CAN STAY TOGETHER.

147
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:21,474
Shannon: ROBIN DID NOT
WANNA BUDGE.

148
00:07:21,474 --> 00:07:23,076
SHE DID NOT WANNA GO
ALONG WITH HER.

149
00:07:23,076 --> 00:07:24,477
Elyse: SO SHE'S GONNA HAVE TO
COMPROMISE AND GO SHOPPING

150
00:07:24,477 --> 00:07:26,346
WITH US, AND WE'RE GONNA
HAVE TO COMPROMISE

151
00:07:26,346 --> 00:07:28,181
AND GO TO THE GRAVE WITH HER.

152
00:07:28,181 --> 00:07:31,017
Robin: AND I SAID
I WANNA GO SHOPPING.

153
00:07:31,017 --> 00:07:31,751
Elyse: YOU'RE NOT WILLING
TO GO TO JIM MORRISON'S GRAVE

154
00:07:31,751 --> 00:07:33,386
FOR ADRIANNE?

155
00:07:33,386 --> 00:07:37,190
Robin: THIS CONVERSATION
CAN GO ON ALL NIGHT.

156
00:07:37,190 --> 00:07:38,758
Elyse: BECAUSE
YOU WON'T COMPROMISE.

157
00:07:38,758 --> 00:07:40,260
Robin: RESPECT ME WHEN I SAY
THAT I DON'T WANNA GO SEE

158
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:41,695
THE GRAVE.

159
00:07:41,695 --> 00:07:44,064
JUST RESPECT ME FOR THAT,
JUST LIKE I RESPECT YOU.

160
00:07:44,064 --> 00:07:45,131
Adrianne: I DIDN'T WANNA
LISTEN TO WHAT THAT BITCH

161
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:46,299
HAD TO SAY.

162
00:07:46,299 --> 00:07:47,634
SHE WAS--SHE'S PSYCHOTIC.

163
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:49,035
Robin: I SAID
I WANNA GO SHOPPIN'.

164
00:07:49,035 --> 00:07:50,570
SHANNON SAID
SHE WANNA GO SHOPPIN'.

165
00:07:50,570 --> 00:07:51,738
Elyse: IT JUST SUCKS THAT I'M
THE ONE WHO HAS TO COMPROMISE

166
00:07:51,738 --> 00:07:53,039
AND YOU GUYS DON'T.

167
00:07:53,039 --> 00:07:54,474
Robin: I DON'T GO SEE GRAVES.

168
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,710
JUST LIKE YOU DON'T BELIEVE
IN GOD, I DON'T GO SEE GRAVES.

169
00:07:56,710 --> 00:07:59,245
I DON'T TRY TO MAKE YOU
BELIEVE IN GOD, DO I?

170
00:07:59,245 --> 00:08:01,348
Elyse: I GOT REALLY UPSET
WHEN I SAW THIS STUBBORN,

171
00:08:01,348 --> 00:08:03,316
BITCHY SIDE OF ROBIN.

172
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:07,120
I SORT OF FLED AWAY FROM HER.

173
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:07,550
Adrianne: WHAT?

174
00:08:08,655 --> 00:08:10,123
Elyse: SHE'S SUCH A BITCH.

175
00:08:10,123 --> 00:08:12,158
Adrianne: WHO IS A BITCH?

176
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:13,493
Elyse: (sniffles) ROBIN.

177
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:15,729
Adrianne: I JUST--
DUDE, SERIOUSLY--

178
00:08:15,729 --> 00:08:18,131
Elyse: SHE'S SO MEAN TO YOU,
AND SHE'S SO MEAN TO ME.

179
00:08:18,131 --> 00:08:20,233
I THINK I WAS CRYING
MAINLY OUT OF FRUSTRATION,

180
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:22,969
BECAUSE ROBIN
WOULDN'T SEE THINGS MY WAY

181
00:08:22,969 --> 00:08:25,505
AND WAS BEING SO INTOLERANT.

182
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:27,574
IT REALLY PISSED ME OFF.

183
00:08:27,574 --> 00:08:31,444
Robin: IT'S FOUR PEOPLE
WITH FOUR DIFFERENT THINGS

184
00:08:31,444 --> 00:08:33,546
THAT THEY WANNA DO
AND HAVING TO COMPROMISE IT

185
00:08:33,546 --> 00:08:35,582
INTO TWO GROUPS.

186
00:08:35,582 --> 00:08:36,616
IT'S NOT DUMB.

187
00:08:36,616 --> 00:08:38,183
IT'S JUST CALLED
A DIFFERENCE OF OPINION,

188
00:08:38,183 --> 00:08:40,453
AND YOU TRY TO MAKE
THE BEST OF IT.

189
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:42,522
Adrianne: ONE DAY
SHE'S GONNA GO AGAINST SOMEBODY

190
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:44,691
THAT DOES NOT CARE
HOW MUCH MONEY YOU HAVE

191
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:47,193
OR HOW MUCH MOMMY AND DADDY
HAVE GIVEN YOU,

192
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:49,562
AND SHE'S GONNA GET HER...

193
00:08:49,562 --> 00:08:51,998
THAT'S JUST HOW IT IS.

194
00:08:51,998 --> 00:08:55,368
THE WORD SAYS THAT
IF YOU ARE STANDING THERE

195
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:56,536
AND SOMEBODY ASKS YOU
FOR YOUR COAT,

196
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:58,571
YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO GIVE IT,
YOU KNOW?

197
00:08:58,571 --> 00:09:01,307
'CAUSE YOU'RE A "CHRISTIAN."

198
00:09:01,307 --> 00:09:04,344
CHRISTIANS ARE NOT SELFISH.

199
00:09:04,344 --> 00:09:06,112
Elyse: SHE DON'T GO SEE
GRAVES.

200
00:09:06,112 --> 00:09:07,747
Adrianne: SHE DOESN'T SEEM
VERY CHRIST-LIKE TO ME.

201
00:09:07,747 --> 00:09:10,717
IN FACT, I THINK SHE SECRETLY
WORSHIPS THE DEVIL.

202
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:13,219
ALL THIS STUFF
SHE'S PRETENDING TO BE--

203
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:15,755
IF, YOU KNOW, THERE REALLY IS
THIS BIG, WONDERFUL MAN

204
00:09:15,755 --> 00:09:19,092
IN THE SKY,
THEN HE'S GONNA WHUP HER ASS

205
00:09:19,092 --> 00:09:21,561
WHEN SHE GETS UP THERE.

206
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:23,129
Elyse: I WAS TRYING
TO KEEP IT FROM BECOMING

207
00:09:23,129 --> 00:09:24,731
YOU AND ME
VERSUS THE TWO OF THEM,

208
00:09:24,731 --> 00:09:27,267
BUT THAT'S IT.

209
00:09:32,972 --> 00:09:38,511
♪♪♪

210
00:09:38,511 --> 00:09:40,080
Elyse: OH, LOOK,
IT'S THAT WAY.

211
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:42,549
AFTER THE FIGHT
IN THE HOTEL ROOM,

212
00:09:42,549 --> 00:09:45,418
OUR GROUP COMPLETELY POLARIZED
INTO US VERSUS THEM.

213
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:48,721
ADRIANNE WANTED TO GO SEE
JIM MORRISON'S GRAVE.

214
00:09:48,721 --> 00:09:50,723
Adrianne: OOH.
DISCOTHEQUE.

215
00:09:50,723 --> 00:09:52,692
Elyse: AND ROBIN AND SHANNON
WANTED TO GO SHOPPING.

216
00:09:52,692 --> 00:09:54,394
Shannon: THIS IS
GONNA BE FUN.

217
00:09:54,394 --> 00:09:56,429
Robin: THIS IS OUR--
ONLY OUR ONE DAY IN PARIS

218
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:58,031
TO GET WHATEVER WE WANTED
TO GET DONE DONE.

219
00:09:58,031 --> 00:10:00,133
IT'S BEST JUST TO SPLIT UP.

220
00:10:00,133 --> 00:10:04,571
Shannon: O EST
LE CHAMPS ELYSEES?

221
00:10:04,571 --> 00:10:05,572
MERCI.

222
00:10:05,572 --> 00:10:06,973
Robin: YOU JUST RUN ACROSS.

223
00:10:06,973 --> 00:10:07,740
Shannon: YOU CAN'T
RUN ACROSS THERE.

224
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:10,143
Robin: YEAH, YOU CAN.

225
00:10:10,143 --> 00:10:11,311
Shannon: I AIN'T
RUNNING ACROSS.

226
00:10:11,311 --> 00:10:12,445
Robin: COME ON, COME ON.

227
00:10:12,445 --> 00:10:14,214
Shannon: YOU CAN'T...

228
00:10:14,214 --> 00:10:16,149
Adrianne: THIS IS
JIM MORRISON'S GRAVE, DUDE.

229
00:10:16,149 --> 00:10:19,085
THIS IS SO COOL.

230
00:10:19,085 --> 00:10:21,354
ELYSE DIDN'T WANNA GO SEE
JIM MORRISON'S GRAVE,

231
00:10:21,354 --> 00:10:25,191
BUT SHE SACRIFICED THAT FOR ME,
AND JUST LIKE, THAT'S COOL.

232
00:10:25,191 --> 00:10:27,494
DUDE, ELYSE, I NEED
A BOYFRIEND FOR THIS PLACE.

233
00:10:27,494 --> 00:10:28,661
WILL YOU BE MY BOYFRIEND?

234
00:10:28,661 --> 00:10:30,330
Elyse: YES, MADAME.

235
00:10:30,330 --> 00:10:31,498
Robin: I THINK IT'S THIS WAY.

236
00:10:31,498 --> 00:10:33,266
COME ON.

237
00:10:33,266 --> 00:10:34,267
Shannon: WHERE IS
THE MONUMENT?

238
00:10:34,267 --> 00:10:35,368
WHERE ARE YOU GOING?

239
00:10:35,368 --> 00:10:37,137
Elyse: IS THIS IT?

240
00:10:37,137 --> 00:10:38,571
Adrianne: THIS HAS TO BE IT.

241
00:10:38,571 --> 00:10:40,974
YOU WANNA LOOK AT THOSE SIGNS?

242
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:42,175
Elyse: I DON'T KNOW.
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

243
00:10:42,175 --> 00:10:44,477
Adrianne: THIS IS
SO BEAUTIFUL.

244
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:50,517
♪♪♪

245
00:10:52,085 --> 00:10:54,254
Adrianne: WE'RE LOST
IN THE GRAVEYARD.

246
00:10:54,254 --> 00:10:58,024
Elyse: DID THEY MOVE
JIM MORRISON'S BODY?

247
00:10:58,024 --> 00:11:00,760
Adrianne: OFFICIALLY LOST.

248
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:03,029
WE WENT TO SEE
JIM MORRISON'S GRAVE,

249
00:11:03,029 --> 00:11:05,698
AND WE ENDED UP LOST.

250
00:11:05,698 --> 00:11:08,468
BUT WE WERE JUST HAVING FUN
WITH EACH OTHER.

251
00:11:08,468 --> 00:11:10,003
IT WAS FUN.

252
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:10,470
Elyse: LOOK,
THERE'S A PHOTO PLACE.

253
00:11:10,470 --> 00:11:11,638
LET'S GO IN THERE.

254
00:11:14,174 --> 00:11:17,243
(laughing)

255
00:11:17,243 --> 00:11:18,578
Elyse: WE DECIDED
TO SEPARATE.

256
00:11:18,578 --> 00:11:19,646
ADRIANNE AND I DID OUR THING.

257
00:11:19,646 --> 00:11:22,415
ROBIN AND SHANNON
WENT TO THE GAP,

258
00:11:22,415 --> 00:11:24,284
AND IN RETROSPECT,
I DON'T KNOW WHY

259
00:11:24,284 --> 00:11:27,320
I WANTED THE FOUR OF US
TO STAY TOGETHER AT ALL.

260
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:29,355
Robin: DO YOU REMEMBER
THE NAME OF THE HOTEL?

261
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:31,124
DID YOU WRITE IT DOWN?

262
00:11:31,124 --> 00:11:33,760
I THOUGHT I ASKED YOU
TO GO AND GET THE NAME OF IT.

263
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:34,661
Shannon: I HAVE IT
ON THAT PIECE OF PAPER,

264
00:11:34,661 --> 00:11:35,528
BUT I DON'T KNOW WHERE I PUT IT.

265
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:37,096
Robin: HERE, COME ON.

266
00:11:37,096 --> 00:11:38,131
Shannon: SOME THINGS
ROBIN DOES MIGHT...

267
00:11:38,131 --> 00:11:41,000
GET ON MY NERVES
AFTER A LITTLE WHILE.

268
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,101
Robin: COME ON, SHANNON.
YOU GOTTA GO FASTER.

269
00:11:49,676 --> 00:11:52,378
Shannon: OKAY, IT SAYS,
"YOU HAVE UNTIL 4 P.M.

270
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:56,216
TO GET READY FOR
A SPECTACULAR NIGHT OUT."

271
00:11:56,216 --> 00:11:58,484
IT SAYS BE READY AT 4 P.M.,
HAIR AND MAKEUP DONE.

272
00:11:58,484 --> 00:12:00,186
IT'S FOR
A SPECTACULAR NIGHT OUT.

273
00:12:00,186 --> 00:12:04,657
♪♪♪

274
00:12:06,159 --> 00:12:07,527
Shannon: ANYONE KNOW
WHAT TIME IT IS?

275
00:12:07,527 --> 00:12:09,395
Elyse: YEAH, IT IS--
Adrianne: WE HAVE 15 MINUTES.

276
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:10,396
Shannon: YOU'RE LYING.

277
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:11,464
Adrianne and Elyse: NOPE.

278
00:12:11,464 --> 00:12:13,266
Shannon: HOLY POOP.

279
00:12:13,266 --> 00:12:14,968
Robin: CAN YOU POP THE TRUNK?

280
00:12:14,968 --> 00:12:19,505
♪♪♪

281
00:12:26,012 --> 00:12:27,981
Pascal: WELCOME BACK.
Elyse: THANK YOU.

282
00:12:50,236 --> 00:12:52,205
Shannon: I'M GONNA BE SCARED
TO WEAR ONE OF YOUR DRESSES.

283
00:12:52,205 --> 00:12:56,676
♪♪♪

284
00:12:56,676 --> 00:12:59,112
Adrianne: THEY GAVE ME
THIS GOWN.

285
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:01,381
THIS GOWN--LIKE, MY BOOBS
WERE HANGING OUT THE SIDE

286
00:13:01,381 --> 00:13:03,750
AND IN THE MIDDLE.

287
00:13:03,750 --> 00:13:07,620
Robin: THE COUTURE CHALLENGE
WAS TO GO OUT WITH SOME MEN

288
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:11,190
AND HAVE THEM JUDGE US
ON BEING A LADY.

289
00:13:11,190 --> 00:13:13,660
WOMEN THAT WEAR COUTURE
ARE SOCIALITES.

290
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:15,295
THEY ARE A LADY IN EVERY SENSE.

291
00:13:28,975 --> 00:13:31,444
Shannon: HI.
Elyse: WE'VE BEEN LIVING
IN REALLY CLOSE QUARTERS

292
00:13:31,444 --> 00:13:33,513
IN OUR MODEL APARTMENT,
AND EVERY SINGLE GIRL

293
00:13:33,513 --> 00:13:36,449
IS FANTASIZING ABOUT SPENDING
A NIGHT AWAY FROM THERE.

294
00:13:36,449 --> 00:13:38,084
Shannon: ARE YOU EXCITED?

295
00:13:38,084 --> 00:13:39,419
ARE YOU EXCITED?

296
00:13:39,419 --> 00:13:42,288
YEAH, YEAH, YEAH, YEAH,
I'M SO EXCITED.

297
00:13:42,288 --> 00:13:45,124
Adrianne: I FEEL SO GOOD
IN THIS.

298
00:13:45,124 --> 00:13:46,192
I FEEL LIKE SOMEBODY ELSE.

299
00:13:49,629 --> 00:13:50,997
Shannon: THERE IT IS.
"FUGUENOT"...

300
00:13:50,997 --> 00:13:52,398
Elyse: WHERE?
Shannon: "FOGO-NOT"...

301
00:13:52,398 --> 00:13:53,399
FOUGU-NUT'S.

302
00:13:53,399 --> 00:13:55,068
Adrianne: FOUGU-NUT'S!

303
00:13:55,068 --> 00:13:57,036
Elyse: I THINK IT'S, LIKE,
FON-GWE?

304
00:13:57,036 --> 00:13:58,438
Man: WELCOME
TO THE FOUQUET'S,

305
00:13:58,438 --> 00:14:00,039
THE OLDER RESTAURANT IN PARIS.

306
00:14:00,039 --> 00:14:01,074
WILL YOU FOLLOW ME, PLEASE?

307
00:14:04,110 --> 00:14:07,046
Shannon: HI.
Adrian: HI. HOW ARE YOU?

308
00:14:07,046 --> 00:14:08,181
I'M ADRIAN. NICE TO MEET YOU.

309
00:14:08,181 --> 00:14:09,982
Shannon: I'M SHANNON.
NICE TO MEET YOU.

310
00:14:09,982 --> 00:14:11,217
Elyse: ELYSE.
NICE TO MEET YOU.

311
00:14:11,217 --> 00:14:13,553
Adrianne: I LIKED
THE ADRIAN DUDE, JUST, WELL,

312
00:14:13,553 --> 00:14:15,021
BECAUSE HIS NAME IS ADRIAN.

313
00:14:15,021 --> 00:14:16,155
Shannon: SHANNON.

314
00:14:16,155 --> 00:14:18,024
NICE TO MEET YOU.
Man: NICE TO MEET YOU.

315
00:14:18,024 --> 00:14:20,626
THEY WERE GONNA JUDGE US ON
HOW WE ACTED LIKE A LADY,

316
00:14:20,626 --> 00:14:22,195
SO I WAS LIKE, YOU KNOW,
I CAN DO THIS.

317
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:23,763
I'M, YOU KNOW, I'M A LADY.

318
00:14:23,763 --> 00:14:31,671
♪♪♪

319
00:14:31,671 --> 00:14:33,172
Adrian: FOIE GRAS.

320
00:14:33,172 --> 00:14:34,540
Shannon: FOIE GRAS. OKAY.

321
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:38,244
Adrian: THEY ARE GOOSE
OR DUCK LIVER.

322
00:14:38,244 --> 00:14:41,447
Man: ARE YOU WILLING
TO TRY IT?

323
00:14:41,447 --> 00:14:43,116
Adrianne: OKAY.

324
00:14:43,116 --> 00:14:44,350
LET'S SEE HOW THIS IS.

325
00:14:44,350 --> 00:14:46,619
Man: BON APPéTIT.

326
00:14:46,619 --> 00:14:48,321
Shannon: SO THIS IS
OUR DINNER?

327
00:14:48,321 --> 00:14:52,592
Adrian: THIS IS IT.

328
00:14:52,592 --> 00:14:53,593
Elyse: I ATE EVERYTHING
I WAS SERVED

329
00:14:53,593 --> 00:14:55,661
JUST TO TRY EVERYTHING.

330
00:14:58,698 --> 00:15:00,366
Robin: THE FOOD WAS NASTY.

331
00:15:00,366 --> 00:15:02,101
YOU KNOW, IT WASN'T LIKE ALL,
YOU KNOW, IT WAS CRACKED UP

332
00:15:02,101 --> 00:15:03,336
TO BE.

333
00:15:03,336 --> 00:15:04,537
Man: YOU LIKE IT?

334
00:15:04,537 --> 00:15:05,738
Robin: IT'S DIFFERENT.

335
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:07,206
IT DOESN'T REALLY--
Man: IT'S DIFFERENT.

336
00:15:07,206 --> 00:15:08,307
Adrianne: ROBIN WAS BEING
A BITCH, BITCH, BITCH,

337
00:15:08,307 --> 00:15:09,275
BITCH, BITCH.

338
00:15:09,275 --> 00:15:12,345
SHANNON'S JUST LIKE...

339
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:16,282
SO I WAS LIKE, ALL RIGHT,
I'M GONNA NAB THIS OPPORTUNITY.

340
00:15:24,724 --> 00:15:27,660
Shannon: THIS PLACE IS BIG.

341
00:15:28,261 --> 00:15:29,529
Elyse: AFTER WE LEFT
THE RESTAURANT,

342
00:15:29,529 --> 00:15:33,733
WE WENT TO SEE A BALLET
AT THE OPERA HOUSE IN PARIS.

343
00:15:37,336 --> 00:15:40,473
Adrianne: I DON'T LIKE BALLET.

344
00:15:40,473 --> 00:15:42,742
IT'S LIKE ALL THESE GUYS
ARE LIKE... (humming)

345
00:15:42,742 --> 00:15:44,277
AND DANCING AROUND.

346
00:15:44,277 --> 00:15:46,012
IT'S LIKE, OH, MY GOD.

347
00:15:46,012 --> 00:15:48,080
BUT I DIDN'T SIT THERE
AND BITCH AND COMPLAIN.

348
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:51,017
I JUST TRIED TO KEEP ACTING
LIKE A LADY.

349
00:15:51,017 --> 00:15:54,086
ARE OUR ACCENTS UGLY
TO YOU GUYS, HONESTLY?

350
00:15:54,086 --> 00:15:55,721
AMERICAN ACCENTS--ARE THEY UGLY?

351
00:15:55,721 --> 00:15:58,991
BE... HONEST.

352
00:15:58,991 --> 00:16:00,359
Man: NO, IT'S NOT UGLY.

353
00:16:00,359 --> 00:16:01,494
YOU JUST GOTTA GET USED TO IT.

354
00:16:01,494 --> 00:16:03,196
Adrianne: IS IT HARSH?

355
00:16:03,196 --> 00:16:04,330
Adrian: (Southern accent)
WELL, I WAS BORN DOWN SOUTH

356
00:16:04,330 --> 00:16:06,632
IN TEXAS.

357
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:09,168
Man: LET'S GO AND PARTY
ALL NIGHT LONG.

358
00:16:09,168 --> 00:16:12,271
Robin: THESE CAT DADDY
LUSTFUL TYPE OF MEN WERE THERE.

359
00:16:12,271 --> 00:16:14,574
YOU COULD TELL
BY THEIR CONVERSATION,

360
00:16:14,574 --> 00:16:16,309
THEY WANTED TO SOCIALIZE,
AND THAT'S THE REASON WHY

361
00:16:16,309 --> 00:16:19,178
I TUNED THEM OUT.

362
00:16:19,178 --> 00:16:20,646
Adrianne: THAT'S ALL SHE DID
FOR, LIKE, FOUR HOURS

363
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:22,181
WITH THESE DUDES,
WAS READ THE BIBLE.

364
00:16:26,586 --> 00:16:30,490
♪♪♪

365
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:33,659
Shannon: OH, PRETTY.

366
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:35,228
WOW.

367
00:16:35,228 --> 00:16:38,464
LOOK, CHOCOLATE.

368
00:16:40,433 --> 00:16:42,401
Adrianne: OH, MY...

369
00:16:42,401 --> 00:16:47,673
Shannon: OH, MY WORD!

370
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:49,442
Shannon: BEAUTIFUL.

371
00:16:49,442 --> 00:16:51,744
Elyse: IT'S HUGE.

372
00:16:51,744 --> 00:16:53,279
WHEN I SAW
THE PRESIDENTIAL SUITE,

373
00:16:53,279 --> 00:16:56,682
UM, I WAS REALLY ATTRACTED
TO IT, BUT I KNEW

374
00:16:56,682 --> 00:17:00,119
THAT EITHER WAY,
SEPARATING MYSELF AND ADRIANNE

375
00:17:00,119 --> 00:17:03,322
FROM ROBIN AND SHANNON
WOULD HAVE BEEN A PRIZE.

376
00:17:03,322 --> 00:17:05,223
Shannon: I BET THIS BED
COULD FIT ALL OF US.

377
00:17:05,223 --> 00:17:06,092
(laughter)
Shannon: NO, REALLY.

378
00:17:06,092 --> 00:17:07,460
NO LYIN'.

379
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,395
Adrianne: WE STEPPED IN,
AND IT WAS JUST IMMACULATE.

380
00:17:09,395 --> 00:17:12,031
IT WAS A PALACE--
A PALACE THAT HAD "ADRIANNE"

381
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:13,332
WRITTEN ALL OVER IT.

382
00:17:13,332 --> 00:17:14,634
Shannon: OH, MY WORD!

383
00:17:14,634 --> 00:17:16,135
Adrianne: OHH!

384
00:17:19,438 --> 00:17:21,007
All: CHEERS.

385
00:17:21,207 --> 00:17:23,009
Elyse: I THOUGHT THAT ROBIN
WOULD EASILY DOMINATE

386
00:17:23,009 --> 00:17:25,978
THE ETIQUETTE COMPETITION,
BUT, UM, SHE WASN'T WILLING

387
00:17:25,978 --> 00:17:28,981
TO MAKE CONVERSATION AT ALL,
SO I THINK THAT, UM,

388
00:17:28,981 --> 00:17:30,283
DEFINITELY DETRACTED
FROM HER PERFORMANCE

389
00:17:30,283 --> 00:17:31,551
IN THE COMPETITION.

390
00:17:31,551 --> 00:17:34,086
Man: ALL RIGHT, LADIES,
WE CAME TO A POINT WHERE WE

391
00:17:34,086 --> 00:17:38,624
HAVE TO MAKE A DECISION ABOUT
WHO'S GONNA BE THE WINNER.

392
00:17:38,624 --> 00:17:41,327
WOULD YOU EXCUSE US FOR, UH,
SOME MINUTES?

393
00:17:41,327 --> 00:17:43,229
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

394
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:45,398
♪♪♪

395
00:17:51,437 --> 00:17:53,039
Man: LET'S START WITH ROBIN.

396
00:17:53,039 --> 00:17:54,540
Adrian: I WOULDN'T VOTE
FOR ROBIN.

397
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:58,010
SHE DIDN'T LIVE UP
TO THIS SOCIAL SCENE

398
00:17:58,010 --> 00:18:00,479
IN TERMS OF THE DISCUSSION
OF BEING INTERESTED

399
00:18:00,479 --> 00:18:02,248
IN OTHER PEOPLE'S INTERESTS.

400
00:18:02,248 --> 00:18:03,349
Man #2: ROBIN, YES.

401
00:18:03,349 --> 00:18:05,751
SHE DIDN'T EAT ANYTHING.

402
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:08,087
Man: BY FRENCH STANDARDS,
IT'S A PROBLEM.

403
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,221
All: (laughing)

404
00:18:09,221 --> 00:18:10,289
Man #3: ADRIANNE IS

405
00:18:10,289 --> 00:18:12,592
VERY FUNNY, BRILLIANT, SMILEY.

406
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:14,727
Adrian: I WOULD SAY
SHE'S MAYBE LESS CLEVER

407
00:18:14,727 --> 00:18:18,698
OR LESS WITTY THAN ELYSE.

408
00:18:18,698 --> 00:18:20,333
Man #2: I LOVE ELYSE,
BECAUSE SHE IS

409
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:22,234
THE CHARMING GIRL.

410
00:18:22,234 --> 00:18:24,503
Adrian: I THINK OF THE FOUR,
SHE'S VERY INTERESTING.

411
00:18:24,503 --> 00:18:26,038
SHE HAS A LOT TO SAY.

412
00:18:26,038 --> 00:18:27,106
Man: SHANNON.

413
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:29,308
Man #2: I LOVE HER FACE,
HER TEETH.

414
00:18:29,308 --> 00:18:30,543
Adrian: BEAUTIFULLY DRESSED.

415
00:18:30,543 --> 00:18:33,079
I THINK SHE DID A GREAT JOB
WEARING THAT DRESS

416
00:18:33,079 --> 00:18:35,448
AND LIVING UP TO THE STANDARDS.

417
00:18:35,448 --> 00:18:39,552
Man #3: I THINK SOMETHING,
UH, SOMETHING, UH, COLD.

418
00:18:39,552 --> 00:18:40,653
Man: SO WE'VE COME
TO A CONCLUSION.

419
00:18:44,657 --> 00:18:46,659
Man: ELYSE, SHANNON,

420
00:18:46,659 --> 00:18:49,695
ROBIN, ADRIANNE,
THANK YOU VERY MUCH

421
00:18:49,695 --> 00:18:52,264
FOR THIS WONDERFUL EVENING.

422
00:18:52,264 --> 00:18:55,968
AS WE SAY, ALL GOOD THING
COME TO AN END.

423
00:18:55,968 --> 00:19:02,141
SO WE HAD THE DIFFICULT MISSION
TO SELECT ONE PERSON, ONE GIRL,

424
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:07,146
AND THE PERSON WE'VE ATTAINED
IS ADRIANNE.

425
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:10,149
CONGRATULATIONS.

426
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:15,054
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE TO GIVE
ONE NAME AMONG YOUR FRIEND.

427
00:19:15,054 --> 00:19:16,555
WHO'S GONNA BE STAYING WITH YOU?

428
00:19:16,555 --> 00:19:17,590
Adrianne: ELYSE.

429
00:19:17,590 --> 00:19:18,691
Man: CONGRATULATIONS.

430
00:19:18,691 --> 00:19:19,725
Shannon: OH, 'LYSA!

431
00:19:19,725 --> 00:19:21,127
Man #2: CAN WE GIVE YOU
A KISS?

432
00:19:21,127 --> 00:19:24,263
(laughter)

433
00:19:24,263 --> 00:19:25,398
Adrianne: LOOK AT THIS SUITE!

434
00:19:25,398 --> 00:19:26,565
SUITE!

435
00:19:26,565 --> 00:19:27,600
I TOLD YOU, I RUINED YOUR DAY.

436
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:29,402
I WAS SO SORRY.

437
00:19:29,402 --> 00:19:33,072
I WAS SO SORRY,
BUT JIM MORRISON IS SO COOL.

438
00:19:33,072 --> 00:19:34,440
Shannon: I THOUGHT
ROBIN WAS GONNA WIN IT BECAUSE

439
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:36,509
SHE'S BEEN TO, LIKE,
ETIQUETTE CLASS.

440
00:19:36,509 --> 00:19:38,277
YOU KNOW, SHE CAN JUST--
SHE'S GOT THAT WHOLE THING.

441
00:19:38,277 --> 00:19:43,182
♪♪♪

442
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:44,283
Elyse: ADRIANNE AND I

443
00:19:44,283 --> 00:19:45,718
HAD A LOT OF FUN
IN THE PRESIDENTIAL SUITE

444
00:19:45,718 --> 00:19:48,354
AFTER OUR ESCORTS LEFT.

445
00:19:48,354 --> 00:19:51,157
Adrianne: LET'S GO EAT
SOME MORE OF THAT CAKE.

446
00:19:51,157 --> 00:19:52,224
YOU KNOW WHAT?

447
00:19:52,224 --> 00:19:54,593
I KNOW HOW TO WORK THE MEN!

448
00:19:54,593 --> 00:19:56,595
Shannon: WE'RE BACK!
